cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying paper, please cite both as below."
title: "block-product-kernel-concentration"
abstract: >
  Reproducibility repository for "Concentration of Block-Product Quantum
  Fidelity Kernels: Exact Theory and Experimental Validation." Proves a sharp,
  non-asymptotic interval for the second-moment concentration exponent of
  block-product fidelity quantum kernels, gives the exact closed form under a
  2-design specialization, separates the kernel's variance-decay exponent from
  the practical shot-noise ranking-collapse threshold, and validates every
  claim against a theoretical contract frozen before any validation code was
  written.
